From dee152823f20724888f1806b5e5fa981e673a3ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 23:25:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(process): recovery never adopts a held
 foreground command (989239fff3)

Recovery checked only _running, so a same-registry pass adopted a survivable
foreground command the terminal tool was still waiting on; its background
reader then reported lost/-1 for a call that exited 0. Release also rewrote
processes.json while the call's .log/.exit still existed, so the merge kept
the released entry as an adoptable worker handoff.

- recovery skips ids held in _foreground_holds (under the registry lock)
- release drops the hold and its entry (drop_ids) in one step under the
  checkpoint file lock; convert_foreground moves hold->_running under it too
- _track_started refuses (ERROR log) to track a still-held command
- tests: same-registry recovery, recovery racing release, release with
  log/exit present, adoption-boundary detection; controls for dead owner
  and deliberate handoff
---
